import re

with open('manuscript.html', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    html = f.read()

cap1 = '<strong>Fig. 1</strong> Bioinformatic pipeline and data deduplication flowchart. Schematic representation of training screening (GSE55763), effect-size filtering, promoter region restriction (TSS200/TSS1500), TCGA clinical deduplication, median-split Kaplan-Meier modeling, and machine learning diagnostic validation. Blue rounded boxes indicate processing milestones connected by directional workflow arrows. Row 1 details differential methylation screening of 839 CpG sites in GSE55763 (n = 2,711), isolating 214 promoter CpG sites passing two-tailed Welch\'s t-tests (p &lt; 0.05) and effect-size filtering (RMSD &ge; 0.5 &times; |&Delta;Beta|). Row 2 details clinical record deduplication of 5,207 longitudinal entries across 470 cases in TCGA-SKCM, matching 395 patient methylation profiles to build the final 24-CpG prognostic panel.'
cap2 = '<strong>Fig. 2</strong> Multi-panel Kaplan-Meier overall survival curves across top prognostic promoter CpG loci (n = 395). Survival curves comparing high (blue solid line and shaded 95% confidence interval) versus low (red solid line and shaded 95% confidence interval) promoter methylation groups stratified at median beta-value. (A) ZCCHC11 (cg00754357, log-rank p = 4.52 &times; 10⁻⁵): High methylation (blue) extends median overall survival from 4.49 years to 9.76 years by silencing pre-let-7 uridylating oncogene TUT4. (B) KMO (cg00606312, log-rank p = 1.00 &times; 10⁻⁴): High methylation extends median survival from 5.09 to 8.92 years by preventing immunosuppressive kynurenine synthesis. (C) EPHA10 (cg00667938, log-rank p = 3.70 &times; 10⁻³): High methylation extends median survival from 5.28 to 8.60 years by dampening RTK signaling. (D) RGS21 (cg00158654, log-rank p = 5.20 &times; 10⁻³): High methylation (blue) reduces median survival from 9.37 years to 5.23 years by silencing GPCR-dampening tumor suppressor. (E) CYMP (cg00076797, log-rank p = 8.00 &times; 10⁻³): High methylation reduces median survival from 9.25 to 5.28 years. (F) AMPD2 (cg00177290, log-rank p = 2.78 &times; 10⁻²): High methylation reduces median survival from 9.37 to 5.23 years by rewiring purine pools.'
cap3 = '<strong>Fig. 3</strong> Absolute promoter methylation distributions in normal controls vs. melanoma tumors. Boxplots with overlayed sample jitter points comparing quantitative promoter CpG methylation beta-values (ranging from 0.0 unmethylated to 1.0 fully methylated) between non-diseased normal controls (left blue boxes) and cutaneous melanoma tumors (right reddish-purple boxes). Top row displays silenced tumor suppressors (RGS21, AMPD2, CYMP, LPPR4) undergoing near-universal hypermethylation in melanoma tumors (mean &beta; &gt; 0.75; &gt; 95% methylated) relative to unmethylated normal controls (&beta; &lt; 0.20). Bottom row displays activated oncogenes (KMO, EPHA10, WNT2B, RAB13) exhibiting severe promoter hypomethylation in melanoma tumors (mean &beta; &lt; 0.15; &gt; 87% demethylated) relative to methylated normal controls (&beta; &gt; 0.75).'
cap4 = '<strong>Fig. 4</strong> Pharmacological and pathway bypass strategies for clinically targeting epigenetic alterations. Dual-column intervention schematic contrasting hypomethylated/active oncogenes (left red container) with hypermethylated/silenced tumor suppressors (right green container). Left column details locus-specific oncogene silencing nodes: ZCCHC11 (targeted by RNAi/ASOs to restore let-7 processing), KMO (small-molecule inhibitors Ro 61-8048 to block kynurenine production), EPHA10 (ADCs targeting extracellular domains), WNT2B (Porcupine inhibitor LGK974 to block Wnt/&beta;-catenin signaling), and RAB13 (geranylgeranyl transferase inhibitors). Right column details pathway compensation nodes for lost tumor suppressors: RGS21 loss (compensated by BRAF/MEK inhibitors dabrafenib/trametinib to dampen GPCR hyperactivity), LPPR4 loss (LPA antagonists to counteract Wnt activation), and AMPD2 loss (methotrexate to inhibit purine synthesis rewiring).'
cap5 = '<strong>Fig. 5</strong> Machine learning classifier performance on primary training set (10-fold cross-validation, n = 790). Horizontal grouped bar chart comparing 10-fold stratified cross-validation classification accuracy on the primary training set (blue bars) against holdout validation accuracy on the independent external GSE105191 cohort (n = 40, green bars) across six machine learning algorithms. Blue bars represent internal 10-fold CV performance (ranging from 88.86% for HistGradientBoosting to 92.15% for Logistic Regression). Green bars represent generalization accuracy on unseen external validation tissue (ranging from 92.50% to 95.00%). All models demonstrate strong discrimination without overfitting.'
cap6 = '<strong>Fig. 6</strong> Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curves and Gain Ratio feature importance. (A) Multi-model ROC curves evaluated on the unseen independent external validation cohort (GSE105191, n = 40; 20 melanoma vs. 20 normal controls). All six model curves (blue, orange, green, red, purple, and brown solid lines) hug the top-left corner of the ROC space (Sensitivity = 1.0, 1 - Specificity = 0.0), far exceeding random chance (grey diagonal dashed line, AUC = 0.50). HistGradientBoosting, Logistic Regression, Naïve Bayes, and MLP achieve AUC = 0.9800, SPegasos SVM achieves AUC = 0.9825, and Random Forest achieves AUC = 0.9600. (B) Horizontal bar chart ranking the top 10 diagnostic promoter CpG descriptors by Gain Ratio score (GainRatioAttributeEval). Bar colors transition along a viridis gradient from dark purple (highest Gain Ratio: AMPD2 cg00177290, Score = 0.1537) to teal (WNT2B, RAB13, ZCCHC11) and yellow-green (HNRNPU cg00533390, Score = 0.0278).'

html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 1</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap1}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)
html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 2</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap2}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)
html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 3</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap3}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)
html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 4</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap4}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)
html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 5</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap5}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)
html = re.sub(r'<div class="fig-caption"><strong>Fig\. 6</strong>.*?</div>', f'<div class="fig-caption">{cap6}</div>', html, flags=re.DOTALL)

with open('manuscript.html', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html)
print('Updated manuscript.html captions successfully!')
